  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to strengthen the conservation of endemic and globally threatened species in Gansu Province, China, which is known for its diverse landscapes and important natural reserves. Infrastructure development, unsustainable land management, and climate change pose threats to forest connectivity and key species populations. The project will address barriers such as inadequate legal framework, weak enforcement, limited management capacities, and insufficient knowledge management. The out</narrative>
